Load Balancers in DevOps Networking
 
Think of a load balancer like a receptionist at a busy office. They greet visitors and send them to the right person, so no one gets overwhelmed.
 
In DevOps, a load balancer directs user traffic to different servers. This keeps your app fast and reliable, even when many people visit at once.
 
It sends requests only to servers that are healthy and ready.
 
Load balancers help your app stay up and running smoothly.
